.TH SDL_GetJoystickPowerInfo 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetJoystickPowerInfo \- Get the battery state of a joystick.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_joystick.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_PowerState SDL_GetJoystickPowerInfo(SDL_Joystick *joystick, int *percent);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
You should never take a battery status as absolute truth\[char46] Batteries (especially failing batteries) are delicate hardware, and the values reported here are best estimates based on what that hardware reports\[char46] It\(aqs not uncommon for older batteries to lose stored power much faster than it reports, or completely drain when reporting it has 20 percent left, etc\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I joystick
the joystick to query\[char46]
.TP
.I percent
a pointer filled in with the percentage of battery life left, between 0 and 100, or NULL to ignore\[char46] This will be filled in with -1 we can\(aqt determine a value or there is no battery\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the current battery state or
.BR SDL_POWERSTATE_ERROR
on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

